     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe. Metformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day, which is twice the usual maximum.\n\n- **Daily maximum:** The FDA-labeled maximum for immediate-release metformin is 2,550 mg/day. Extended-release is capped at 2,000\u20132,500 mg/day.\n- **Single dose:** The usual maximum is 850\u20131,000 mg per dose. 1,700 mg in one dose is above that.\n- **Risk:** Doses this high raise the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nWas one of these intended?\n- **850 mg three times daily** (2,550 mg/day), which is the usual maximum.\n- **1,700 mg/day**, given as 850 mg twice daily.\n- Another dose, such as 500 mg or 1,000 mg per dose.\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it right away. If 1,700 mg three times daily is intentional, please confirm that. I'd suggest adding a clinical rationale to the order note."
      }
     ],
